From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hwmon-temp: skip PECI auxiliary devices before I2C parsing

The hwmon scan includes PECI CPU and DIMM temperature inputs. Their device
names are auxiliary device names, not I2C bus-address pairs, so passing them
to getDeviceBusAddr produces misleading "found bad device" errors for every
input on every rescan. These temperatures are handled by ceb-gnrd-temp-max
on this board. Skip these known auxiliary device types before I2C parsing;
retain malformed I2C device diagnostics and normal temperature discovery.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific PECI sensor ownership]
---
--- a/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp
+++ b/src/hwmon-temp/HwmonTempMain.cpp
@@ -333,6 +333,16 @@
                     deviceName = device.stem();
                 }
 
+                // PECI auxiliary devices are not I2C bus-address pairs.
+                // Their CPU/DIMM inputs belong to ceb-gnrd-temp-max.
+                if (deviceName.starts_with("peci_cpu.cputemp.") ||
+                    deviceName.starts_with("peci_cpu.dimmtemp."))
+                {
+                    lg2::debug("Skipping PECI auxiliary device '{NAME}'",
+                               "NAME", deviceName);
+                    continue;
+                }
+
                 uint64_t bus = 0;
                 uint64_t addr = 0;
                 if (!getDeviceBusAddr(deviceName, bus, addr))
